*.tmp
__pycache__/

# raw/ is deliberately NOT ignored. It was, until 2026-08-20, on the theory
# that per-run JSON is regenerable noise. It is not: alert emails cannot be
# re-fetched, ledger records carry only a slim subset of each listing's
# fields, and a run that drops a harvest file leaves that file as the only
# surviving copy of the data. Committing raw/ is what makes a bad run cost a
# `git checkout` instead of a permanent hole.
